== casting 1 / FR-037: what this casting touched, and what the tree shows ==

  ADDRESS NOTE. The casting prompt Verification section names
  tests/test_orchestrator_gates.py, which casting 2 carved into
  tests/orchestration/. The package-wide AST and import scans that
  parenthetical is about now live in
  tests/orchestration/test_module_boundaries.py, so that is the file this log
  drives in its place. The claim is unchanged; only its address moved.

  WHAT CHANGED THIS CYCLE. Three defects, all LIVE, all inside this castings
  own two modules.

  fallout D-071 / AC-032 -- BOTH HALVES OF THE ROSTER GUARD FAILED OPEN ON A
  DOCUMENT THIS DOOR DID NOT STAMP. read_roster tested derived_at not in data
  and answered NO ROSTER, and foundry_roster scoped its write-once door on the
  same field. This runs own rosters/research_audit.json is exactly that shape
  -- items 42, stream, total, and no derived_at -- so a second Foundry-Roster
  write replaced the 42 items with 1 and left revisions empty, which is the
  replace-semantics write that drops history GI-006 names, and Foundry-Stream
  accepted items_total 7 at full coverage because ROSTER_MISMATCH had no length
  to compare with. derived_at is provenance; the items list is what makes a
  document a roster. There are three answers now rather than two: absent, a
  document carrying an items list, and a NAMED problem for anything else at the
  path. The write door scopes on the document itself, and foundry_init and
  migrate-archive.py both create rosters/ and put nothing in it, so no invented
  stub can refuse a real first derivation.

  fallout D-091 / GI-020 -- THE ROSTER_EXISTS HINT NAMED AN EXIT ON NO
  BOUNDARY. Its first remedy read: read it with Foundry-Rosters reader.
  read_roster is a Python function no MCP tool surfaces, so the only actionable
  branch left was revise=True, which REPLACES the roster with the agents
  re-derived list -- GI-020s own named violation. The refusal carries the
  roster now: stream, items, items_total, derived_at and path beside error,
  hint and phase. Every exit the hint names is reachable from the refused
  state: items and path are keys of the same return value, and revise and
  reason are declared properties of the Foundry-Roster input schema that
  server.py passes through.

  fallout D-073 / GI-013 -- THE DOCUMENT RESERVED FOR PROSE DESTROYED PROSE.
  render_concerns_markdown emitted the carry marker only when a tail already
  existed, so a file this module generated with no prose in it had nowhere safe
  to put any: a lead ruling appended below the last entry carried no marker,
  fell into the generated-by-an-earlier-render branch, and was dropped on the
  next write -- while the preamble the same module emits promised the reader
  the opposite, in the same file. The marker is unconditional now, because it
  is where the generated region ENDS and a file only has somewhere safe to
  write prose if the end is marked before there is prose to keep. The previous
  marker spelling is still scanned, since the prose under it in an
  already-generated archive is the only copy.

  NOTHING IS DESELECTED, AND THE SELECTION IS WHOLE. No deselects and no
  qualifications: every rung below runs, and every rung below passes.

  WHAT FR-037 CLAIMS HERE, precisely. This casting touched no file outside its
